**JavaScript & Event Loop:**
JavaScript runs single-threaded on an **event loop** with a call stack, **microtask queue** (`Promise.then`, `await`), and **macrotask queue** (`setTimeout`, I/O).
```js
async function loadJson(url) {
  const res = await fetch(url);
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status}`);
  return await res.json();
}
```
Use **TypeScript** for static types, interfaces, and compile-time safety.
